# Google OAuth client IDs, from https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values — .env is gitignored.
#
# This app uses two different Google sign-in flows depending on platform —
# see src/hooks/useGoogleSignIn.js for why.

# --- Web (used by `expo start --web`) ---
# Client type: "Web application"
#   Authorized redirect URI: http://localhost:8081
# This is a confidential client type, so it also needs its Client Secret
# (shown right next to the Client ID on the same credentials page).
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID_WEB=
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET_WEB=

# --- Native / Expo Go (used on iOS and Android) ---
# Client type: "TVs and Limited Input devices"
# Redirect-based sign-in can't work in Expo Go — Expo shut down the
# auth.expo.io proxy that used to give it a stable redirect URI, and Expo
# Go isn't your app, so it can't own a custom URL scheme for Google to
# redirect back to either. This client type sidesteps the problem entirely:
# no redirect URI at all. Instead, the app shows a short code and a link to
# google.com/device — you open that on any browser, sign in, and enter the
# code. The app polls in the background and picks up the login once you do.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID_TV=
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET_TV=

# Once you're ready to build a real dev client (`npx expo run:ios` / `eas
# build --profile development`), you can switch native back to the regular
# popup flow using per-platform iOS/Android client IDs — ask if you want
# that wired up when the time comes.
